### 1. Get a token (copy access_token into @token below)
POST http://localhost:8180/realms/boxdrawer/protocol/openid-connect/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=password&client_id=boxdrawer-client&username=demo&password=demo

###
@token = PASTE_ACCESS_TOKEN_HERE
@gw = http://localhost:8080

### No token -> 401
GET {{gw}}/api/boards

### Create a board
POST {{gw}}/api/boards
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "My first board" }

### Voice command: grid
POST {{gw}}/api/commands
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "boardId": 1, "text": "draw a grid of 4 by 4 squares" }

### Voice command: link
POST {{gw}}/api/commands
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "boardId": 1, "text": "map square 1 to square 6 label depends on" }

### Command history
GET {{gw}}/api/commands?boardId=1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Get the board
GET {{gw}}/api/boards/1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Tag the board
POST {{gw}}/api/boards/1/tags/important
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Share the board (email appears in http://localhost:8025)
POST {{gw}}/api/boards/1/share
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "friend@example.com" }

### Download the board as Excalidraw
GET {{gw}}/api/boards/1/export
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### One-time share link from the email (no JWT, second call -> 410)
GET {{gw}}/api/shared/PASTE_TOKEN_FROM_EMAIL
